# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, 2.1-7, 2.1-11, R-5). L §5.14 A relabel: "a leg whose two ends are one place that keeps parts.
# It takes parts by the leaving rule and returns them labelled by the arrival rule, batches kept; it books nothing net,
# and flows counts it as 0"; "Whose parts a leg takes is the order's": the order ranks the giver's parts first (if w in
# gifts and k.owner == w.giver then 0 else 1), and the arrival rule gives a gift to its receiver. tomek's 80.00 (inh)
# gives 30.00 to ania: tomek 50.00, ania 30.00, the couple's 100.00 unchanged, the total 180.00 (scratch/exp4.py).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind couples: parties
kind savings: place PLN min 0
  owned by arrive
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w order if w in gifts and k.owner == w.giver then 0 else 1, if k.owner == ania_tomek then 0 else 1
kind gifts: transfers
  attr giver: key persons
  attr receiver: key persons
kind inhs: transfers
place konto: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input wage_day: date
input wage_amt: money PLN
input inh_day: date
input inh_amt: money PLN
input g_day: date
input g_amt: money PLN
def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule community = if p == ania_tomek then 1 else 0
  rule gift beats community = if p == m.receiver then 1 else 0 when m in gifts
  rule inh beats community = if p == tomek then 1 else 0 when m in inhs
move wage: transfers
  on wage_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount wage_amt
move inh: inhs
  on inh_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount inh_amt
move g: gifts
  on g_day
  attr giver = tomek
  attr receiver = ania
  leg cash from konto to konto amount g_amt
ask q: bal(konto, 2026-03-31), bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of ania, bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of tomek, bal(konto, 2026-03-31) of ania_tomek
ask q2: flows(konto, 2026-03), g.cash.amount of tomek

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  couples + [ania_tomek] lives 2010-06-01..
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  wage_day = 2026-02-01
  wage_amt = 100.00 PLN
  inh_day = 2026-02-15
  inh_amt = 80.00 PLN
  g_day = 2026-03-01
  g_amt = 30.00 PLN
=== expect
q: (180.00 PLN, 30.00 PLN, 50.00 PLN, 100.00 PLN)
  cut 2026-01-01
q2: (0.00 PLN, 30.00 PLN)
  cut 2026-01-01
